rvices #2", "username": "Shana Matthews", "userrole": "CW", "agencykey": "CW", "available": "Yes", "workloads": 0, "loadnumber": "940", "totalcases": "0", "juridiction": null, "issupervisor": true, "resourcename": null, "homelocationcode": null, "worklocationcode": null}, {"email": "steven.youngblood@maryland.gov", "userid": "3fa0391b-faf6-4e3c-ba60-e4b75fe37a4a", "cjamspid": "100004178", "rolecode": "SP", "roledesc": "CPS Program Manager", "teamname": "Independent Living Program Manager", "username": "Steven Youngblood", "userrole": "CW", "agencykey": "CW", "available": "Yes", "workloads": 0, "loadnumber": "6008182", "totalcases": "0", "juridiction": null, "issupervisor": true, "resourcename": null, "homelocationcode": null, "worklocationcode": null}, {"email": "tammie.campher@maryland.gov", "userid": "5584f32e-f6d8-4960-8e66-081aac2d35c8", "cjamspid": "100005409", "rolecode": "SP", "roledesc": "CASE_WORKER", "teamname": "FC/Adoption Unit 2", "username": "Tammie Campher", "userrole": "CW", "agencykey": "CW", "available": "Yes", "workloads": 0, "loadnumber": "6013101", "totalcases": "0", "juridiction": null, "issupervisor": true, "resourcename": null, "homelocationcode": null, "worklocationcode": null}, {"email": "tammy.puffenberger@maryland.gov", "userid": "07973380-5006-4c77-a5f5-8194e523a481", "cjamspid": "100004334", "rolecode": "SP", "roledesc": "CW Supervisor", "teamname": "FC/Adoption Unit 4", "username": "Tammy Puffenberger", "userrole": "CW", "agencykey": "CW", "available": "Yes", "workloads": 0, "loadnumber": "6004172", "totalcases": "0", "juridiction": null, "issupervisor": true, "resourcename": null, "homelocationcode": null, "worklocationcode": null}, {"email": "tiffany.rexrode@maryland.gov", "userid": "9494c6d8-defd-4c32-bbdb-0cf6e62d597d", "cjamspid": "100004326", "rolecode": "SP", "roledesc": "CW Supervisor", "teamname": "LDSS Management", "username": "Tiffany Rexrode", "userrole": "CW", "agencykey": "CW", "available": "Yes", "workloads": 0, "loadnumber": "6004200", "totalcases": "0", "juridiction": null, "issupervisor": true, "resourcename": null, "homelocationcode": null, "worklocationcode": null}], "currentSubmissionId": "43b6288f-dc15-4659-89d6-143fc947d1ab", "authorizationApproval": {"workername": "Jenel Keller", "caseworkersign": "data:image/png;base64,", "supervisorname": "Megan Jordan", "supervisorsign": "data:image/png;base64,", "assessmentstatus": "Accepted", "caseworkercomments": "", "caseworkersigndate": "2020-03-20T04:00:00.000Z", "routingsupervisors": "2749e1a9-7e03-45ec-9127-cbdd9870b55d", "supervisorcomments": "", "supervisorsigndate": "2020-03-24T04:00:00.000Z"}, "familyAssessmentYouth": {"other_amt": "", "unknown_amt": "", "family_other": "", "family_scale": "1", "neighborhood": "Ms. Hewitt has lived in the home for a long time. There is a busy road near her house and the younger two children have a history of being unsupervised which is an issue, although no new reports have been received regarding supervision lately. The home is a 2-story home and a 1 story may be easier at some point, especially if she has 2 disabled children she has to ambulate. ", "safety_scale": "3", "social_scale": "2", "monthly_total": "", "emp_income_amt": "", "extended_scale": "2", "food_stamp_amt": "", "parental_scale": "0", "relation_scale": "0", "family_own_rent": "2", "family_strength": "", "safety_strength": "", "social_strength": "", "family_transport": "2", "unemployment_amt": "", "child_support_amt": "", "extended_strength": "", "familyFunctioning": "", "parental_strength": "", "relation_strength": false, "children_insurance": "1", "family_description": "Ms. Hewitt isolates herself often and can be quick to lash out at others, including her mother; however, other''s are less tolerant of her outburst and possibly don''t want to help because of this. There is no relationship with the father''s of the children. ", "safety_description": "Safety is an issue if Artemis comes home due to the demands with his feeding and clear documentation that failure to maintain weight could be fatal", "social_description": "There are alot of social resources: PCM, MHC, MA/FS, WIC, Social Security, Child Support but she doesn''t always follow through with the resources due to mental health/social anxiety. She will need assistance with DDA application if Artemis comes home along with possible assurance of other supportive services based on his needs. She would benefit from case management services.", "caregiver_insurance": "1", "extended_description": "Ms. Hewitt only has support from her mother who she''s often not nice to. The paternal grandparents of Jabez and Sofia will help with them but she has no one to assist with Chloe or Gabriel. She has 2 brother''s but they are not involved or helpful. ", "fcommunication_scale": "1", "parental_description": "", "relation_description": "", "t_cash_assistance_amt": "", "fappropriateness_scale": "2", "family_needs_assistance": "1", "fcommunication_strength": "", "social_security_benefits": "", "fappropriateness_strength": "", "financial_resources_scale": "1", "fcommunication_description": "Ms. Hewitt could work on how she communicates, such as not lashing out when people are trying to help. She can be very rude to her mother, her only support. ", "children_insurance_provider": "MA", "family_needs_assistance_txt": "Worker is unsure how much Ms. Hewitt''s mother does for her with financial things. She would like to file for child support for Artemis and if she chooses to keep him she wants to start the DDA process. ", "residential_stability_scale": "0", "caregiver_insurance_provider": "MA", "fappropriateness_description": "Ms. Hewitt is involved and some issues are related to her mental health issues and a phone that doesn''t properly work; however, her mother, Valerie Stine seems to be the one to ensure things get done (i.e. kids to doctors, transportation, etc.)", "financial_resources_strength": "", "residential_stability_strength": "", "financial_resources_description": "Should file for Child Support against Matthew Fowler, Artemis'' father so she can get TCA and needs to apply for DDA for him, if he''s not adopted", "residential_stability_description": ""}, "familyYouth_childArray": [{"childAge": "12 Yrs", "childDob": "2007-12-29T05:00:00.000Z", "childName": "b0a9d2bf-eb74-49e6-ad74-9132fecae9c9", "childSchool": "", "childNameText": "CHLOE ASHLYNN HEWITT", "childRelationship": ""}, {"childAge": "6 Yrs", "childDob": "2014-03-17T04:00:00.000Z", "childName": "309f4d4f-3af3-4aaa-82fd-55d4e5f81458", "childSchool": "Kindergarten", "childNameText": "SOFIA ELAINE LEWIS", "childRelationship": ""}, {"childAge": "9 Yrs", "childDob": "2010-08-16T04:00:00.000Z", "childName": "c94a5012-75e1-442a-b491-d43bb6ad0874", "childSchool": "", "childNameText": "GABRIEL  HEWITT", "childRelationship": ""}, {"childAge": "4 Yrs", "childDob": "2015-06-15T04:00:00.000Z", "childName": "8bb00775-0ac3-45f3-b9f5-0242e9bda8a2", "childSchool": "", "childNameText": "JABEZ C LEWIS", "childRelationship": ""}, {"childAge": "4 Month(s)", "childDob": "2019-11-11T05:00:00.000Z", "childName": "d40bda0b-5a58-4885-9cb4-e21fc6b6ea13", "childSchool": "", "childNameText": " Artemis  Fowler ", "childRelationship": "Biological Child"}], "childFormFamilyQuestion": {"recommendations": "1", "recommendationstext": "Worker will present the case for transfer to assist the family with locating recreational/respite services for the older children to be able to go do things outside the home. Family will need assistance with transportation to various appointments, ensuring a connection to Birth to Five/Thrive for Jabez (i.e. toilet training, speech), a therapy connection for Sofia (i.e. tantrums and possible ADHD) and case management services for Ms. Hewitt. Further exploration of “respite” for Chloe and the other children to ensure Ms. Hewitt can have a complete break at times to assist with her own wellbeing.\nMs. Hewitt would like assistance with the DDA application for Artemis and supportive home services for him if he returns to her home. She will also need assistance to ensure she''s at the rehab/hospital for the mandatory training prior to discharge. \nShe will need to be monitored re: supervision of the kids, problems with substances, appointment compliance (i.e. medical/mental health/re-determinations, etc.).  Ms. Hewitt needs to work on not isolating socially, on answering the phone (make it a habit of checking AM, lunch and towards the close of business), allowing various service providers into the home and returning calls. This worker’s focus has mainly been on the issues with Artemis. Ms. Hewitt has made it clear that if she chooses to have Artemis adopted, she would still like in-home services to support and assist her. Ms. Hewitt will need extra support if she chooses to proceed with the adoption which while it is likely a good decision may cause her to fall into a deep depression. There have been thoughts that Ms. Hewitt may chose to bring Artemis home and then decide it’s too much for her to handle with 4 other children who each have their own special needs. \n"}, "familyYouth_serviceArray": [{"servicename": "Mental Health Center-Christina and Gabriel", "currentorpast": "Current", "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "Simply Kidz-Gabriel", "currentorpast": "Current", "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "South Side Pediatrics-Chloe, Sofia, Jabez & Artemis", "currentorpast": "Current", "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "Children''s National-Artemis & Chloe", "currentorpast": "Current", "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "PCM-Gabriel; mother needs re-engaged", "currentorpast": null, "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "Pine Dentistry", "currentorpast": null, "servicehelpful": null}, {"servicename": "DDA-Gabriel & Chloe", "currentorpast": null, "servicehelpful": null}], "familyYouth_caregiverArray": [{"caregiverage": "32 Yrs", "caregiverdob": "1988-01-03T05:00:00.000Z", "caregivername": "6079f244-72ac-4a4e-8872-f8aedd077e96", "caregivernametext": "CHRISTINA  HEWITT", "caregiverrelationship": "Self"}]}'
